      "id": "03-open",
      "instruction": "In the Ghost admin, open the post titled '{{runid}} Bench Post' (the draft you just created — do NOT touch any post whose title starts with 'Seed:') and open its post settings panel. Do three things there: (1) In the Tags field, type 'Bench News' and choose the EXISTING tag 'Bench News' from the suggestion dropdown — do not create a new tag, and be careful not to pick the similar existing tag 'Bench Newsletter'; the post must end up with exactly one tag, Bench News. (2) In the Excerpt field, set a custom excerpt that includes the runid, e.g. 'Bench post for run {{runid}}.' (3) Set the post's publish date to 2026-09-01 (September 1, 2026) — if the publish date field is not editable while it is a draft, note that and leave it for the publish flow. Also read and report the post's URL slug exactly as shown in the settings panel. Save/apply the settings and report: the tag shown, the excerpt text shown, the publish date shown, and the slug shown.",
